{
  "methodology": "v1",
  "published": "2026-04-17",
  "description": "Numbers published from the April 2026 run of the v1 harness (4 backends, LangChain 0.2, 5 runs x 50 turns, Claude 4.5 Sonnet via DO Serverless Inference). No v1 run bundle exists; these values were copied from the hand-written README and remotion/src/data/benchmarkData.ts as they stood before v2, and are the only source for both now.",
  "limitations": [
    "Probes were sent as ordinary chat turns, so each probe and answer was written back into memory (flatters later checkpoints).",
    "buffer and summary used LangChain's ConversationChain prompt; qdrant and pgvector used a custom prompt.",
    "Recall turns that collided with seed turns (25 and 35) were silently never probed.",
    "Scoring was substring matching of answer-key words, which both over- and under-counted.",
    "Latency wrapped retrieval, generation and the memory write together; cost used a 75/25 blended token price.",
    "Model responses were not saved, so refusals (Wi-Fi password, bank PIN) could not be told apart from misses."
  ],
